{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Speak, pray</b> — One always accords honor to the kingdom before the priesthood and before prophecy, as [with] Joshua before Caleb. But in the word of HaShem the order is reversed: Caleb first, even though Joshua was greater than Caleb in years; HaShem gave him precedence in speaking of him because of \"and Caleb silenced\" and not \"and Joshua silenced,\" and it is written: \"after Saul and after Samuel.\" They are: David and Samuel founded. And likewise Zerubbabel before Joshua, for he is of the seed of Jehoiachin."], :book :haggai, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The phrase 'אחרי שאול ואחרי שמואל' is hyper-literally rendered; it is unclear whether Saul or a different reading is intended, and the connective to the following clause is compressed."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Haggai" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/hagai"] ["Ibn Ezra on Haggai -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/hagai"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:49:31.357797409Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}